From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sf2000-linux <sf2000-linux@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 08:40:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: use ROM helper presence for SF2000 delay detection

Real hardware may not keep a useful non-zero word visible at the MIPS reset
alias after the stock loader has handed off to the payload. The ROM/FatFS
helper functions in RAM are a better handoff signal: the loader has already
used them successfully when it can update log.txt, while direct blank-ROM QEMU
boots leave that RAM empty.

Use the ROM f_mount helper word to decide whether to compress visible
diagnostic delays. This keeps physical pulses human-visible even if the
0xbfc00000 alias reads back as zero.
---
 arch/mips/kernel/setup.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/mips/kernel/setup.c b/arch/mips/kernel/setup.c
--- a/arch/mips/kernel/setup.c
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/setup.c
@@ -73,7 +73,7 @@ static const char builtin_cmdline[] __initconst = "";
 #endif
 
 #define SF2000_SYSIO_KSEG1 ((volatile unsigned char *)CKSEG1ADDR(0x18800000))
-#define SF2000_BOOTROM_KSEG1 ((volatile unsigned int *)CKSEG1ADDR(0x1fc00000))
+#define SF2000_ROM_F_MOUNT_KSEG0 ((volatile unsigned int *)0x8101f044)
 #define SF2000_PINMUX_L_OFF 0x4a0
 #define SF2000_PINMUX_R_OFF 0x4e0
 #define SF2000_GPIO_L_OUT_OFF 0x54
@@ -99,11 +99,18 @@ static unsigned int __init sf2000_cp0_count(void)
 	return count;
 }
 
+static int __init sf2000_rom_handoff_present(void)
+{
+	unsigned int word = *SF2000_ROM_F_MOUNT_KSEG0;
+
+	return word != 0 && word != 0xffffffffu;
+}
+
 static void __init sf2000_stage_delay(unsigned int ticks)
 {
 	unsigned int start = sf2000_cp0_count();
 
-	if (*SF2000_BOOTROM_KSEG1 == 0)
+	if (!sf2000_rom_handoff_present())
 		ticks >>= SF2000_QEMU_DIRECT_DELAY_SHIFT;
 
 	if (!ticks)
-- 
